	(text "Sensor 1 → PB6: Autonics PNP proximity sensor, PC817 opto input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "881734d7-5d0b-5797-93de-e5e8d88a9ef3")
	)
	(text "J10: 1 = +24 V (brown) through F7 100 mA PTC, 2 = sensor output (black), 3 = 0 V (blue).\nOutput ON (24 V): ≈ 2.3 mA through R24 10k + U6 LED → PB6 HIGH (3.3 V, emitter follower).\nOutput OFF, cable unplugged or broken: PB6 LOW (R25 10k pull-down).\nD18 1N4148W: reverse clamp across the opto LED. C14 100 nF / 50 V: supply decoupling + ESD.\nA shorted sensor cable trips F7 only: the other sensor and the board keep running."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 33.02 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "ab8c01d9-bca8-56c4-9435-faa2bc1a9e20")
	)
	(text "Sensor 2 → PC15: Autonics PNP proximity sensor, PC817 opto input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 78.74 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "0ec87dd2-e95c-5478-bc46-d053a2ba606b")
	)
	(text "J11: 1 = +24 V (brown) through F8 100 mA PTC, 2 = sensor output (black), 3 = 0 V (blue).\nOutput ON (24 V): ≈ 2.3 mA through R26 10k + U7 LED → PC15 HIGH (3.3 V, emitter follower).\nOutput OFF, cable unplugged or broken: PC15 LOW (R27 10k pull-down).\nD19 1N4148W: reverse clamp across the opto LED. C15 100 nF / 50 V: supply decoupling + ESD.\nA shorted sensor cable trips F8 only: the other sensor and the board keep running."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 88.9 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "7b9a38bc-27f6-5445-8d3d-ffbd4821307d")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 15.24 132.08)
		(end 297.18 175.26)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "4257e7b1-cbdb-5e87-9bbf-e9b17c3f5eb7")
	)
	(text "Sensor inputs: notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 134.62 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "f5455157-1577-5802-b5b3-3d49943ae307")
	)
	(text "For 3-wire PNP (sourcing) 24 V sensors, e.g. Autonics PRD08 / PR series (brown +V, black OUT, blue 0 V).\nNPN (sinking) sensors need a different input circuit.\n\nSame circuit as the MES4-Flasher sensor channels 3 / 4 (PB6 / PC15), without the Flasher INA226 supply monitors.\nGPIO budget: all 14 module pins are used (Main sheet, MES4-CIF §2c). More sensors need inputs on\nI²C1, e.g. a TCA9535 expander (0x20-0x27), polled.\n\nPB6: the ST bootloader enables a 25-55 kΩ pull-up on PB6 (blank chip only); with the 10k pull-down it\nreads LOW, which is harmless for an input. PC15: input only (RTC-domain pin, CIF rule 10): fine here.\nInterrupts: PB6 → EXTI6. PC15 shares EXTI15 with PA15 (INA236 ALERT): give EXTI15 to PC15 (sensor 2)\nand poll ALERT, which the INA236 latches (MASK/ENABLE LEN = 1), so no fault is missed.\nNo back-powering: the PC817 collectors run from +3V3_MOD (module finger 4), so nothing drives the\nmodule pins while it is unpowered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 139.7 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "c1cfb5c9-f31f-5d79-8540-e95f66da6002")
	)
